e-matched opaque processes in the returned limitation and cover the count in the regression test.\",\n      \"owner\": \"@pose-maintainers\",\n      \"review_by\": \"2026-12-24\"\n    }\n  ],\n  \"prior_findings\": [\n    {\n      \"id\": \"R4-N2\",\n      \"status\": \"fixed\",\n      \"evidence\": \"pose-mcp/internal/pose/delegation_release.go:66-76\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"R5-N1\",\n      \"status\": \"fixed\",\n      \"evidence\": \"pose-mcp/internal/pose/delegation_release.go:66-76\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"R5-N2\",\n      \"status\": \"fixed\",\n      \"evidence\": \"pose-mcp/internal/pose/delegation_release.go:113-127\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"R5-N3\",\n      \"status\": \"fixed\",\n      \"evidence\": \"pose-mcp/internal/pose/delegation_release.go:141-155\"\n    }\n  ],\n  \"sweep\": \"Swept the sealed change paths across Linux process enumeration/pidfd signaling, dispatch cleanup ordering and safety records, marker/reservation/receipt release and locking, delegate list/cancel/help behavior, attempt ledger and round accounting, review-brief/10 with earlier-template compatibility, English and pt-BR manuals and scaffold copies, and the related regression tests.\",\n  \"criteria\": [\n    {\n      \"id\": \"assumption-integrity\",\n      \"disposition\": \"finding\",\n      \"evidence\": \"N2\",\n      \"rationale\": \"The run-specific environment marker is verified for descendants that retain it, but absence of the marker is treated as proof that no descendant remains; the L1 case where a descendant clears it is not proven to make cleanup fail.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"backend-concurrency\",\n      \"disposition\": \"finding\",\n      \"evidence\": \"N1\",\n      \"rationale\": \"The flock serializes releases, but discarded active-marker read losses allow the confirmation path to bypass proof that a live owner is gone.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"backend-contracts\",\n      \"disposition\": \"passed\",\n      \"evidence\": \"integration:pose-mcp/go/delegation-surface-integration\",\n      \"rationale\": \"The new cancel flag is additive, existing record schemas remain unchanged, and released attempts use ordinary failed run and receipt records.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"backend-input-errors\",\n      \"disposition\": \"finding\",\n      \"evidence\": \"N1\",\n      \"rationale\": \"A corrupt or unreadable marker is not surfaced as a release refusal; the orphan scan treats it as absent.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"backend-integration-impact\",\n      \"disposition\": \"passed\",\n      \"evidence\": \"integration:pose-mcp/go/delegation-surface-integration\",\n      \"rationale\": \"The integration assessment found no changed REST, Protobuf, Kafka, or MCP contract; its three unobserved HTTP declarations are outside this change.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"backend-observability\",\n      \"disposition\": \"finding\",\n      \"evidence\": \"N3\",\n      \"rationale\": \"When an opaque process started during the run, the returned count includes it while the dispatch limitation labels the count as pre-existing.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"compatibility\",\n      \"disposition\": \"passed\",\n      \"evidence\": \"integration:pose-mcp/go/delegation-surface-integration\",\n      \"rationale\": \"Existing CLI arguments and stored record meanings are retained; the new confirmation flag and failed-run receipt are additive.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"correctness\",\n      \"disposition\": \"finding\",\n      \"evidence\": \"N2\",\n      \"rationale\": \"The successful no-match path does not establish that all run-owned descendants ended when a descendant clears the marker and leaves the process group.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"design-causality\",\n      \"disposition\": \"finding\",\n      \"evidence\": \"N2\",\n      \"rationale\": \"D1 correctly addresses commands escaping the adapter process group and D2 preserves attempt history, but D1'\"'s marker can be cleared and the current cleanup path then has no evidence that the process ended.\\\",\n      \\\"mappings\\\": []\n    },\n    {\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"documentation\\\",\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"passed\\\",\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"unit:pose-mcp/go/test\\\",\n      \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"The root and scaffold manuals in both locales describe Linux marker-based reaping, stalled-attempt release, and the explicit legacy confirmation; the brief uses immutable review-brief/10.\\\"\n    },\n    {\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"operability\\\",\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"finding\\\",\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"N1\\\",\n      \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"The cancel path can release despite an unreadable live marker and does not carry the listing loss into the successful named-attempt path.\\\"\n    },\n    {\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"requirements\\\",\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"finding\\\",\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"N2\\\",\n      \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"R1/R2 and the L1 residual require an escaped descendant that cannot be proven ended to keep cleanup incomplete; the marker-cleared path returns success.\\\"\n    },\n    {\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"scope\\\",\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"passed\\\",\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"unit:pose-mcp/go/test\\\",\n      \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"The sealed changed-path list matches the spec artifacts; implementation is confined to review cleanup, abandoned-attempt recovery, CLI/help, brief, and manuals.\\\"\n    },\n    {\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"security\\\",\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"finding\\\",\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"N2\\\",\n      \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"A reviewer-started process can evade the ownership marker and continue after the run while cleanup reports success; the design relies on a mutable process environment.\\\"\n    },\n    {\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"solution-proportionality\\\",\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"finding\\\",\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"N2\\\",\n      \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"The environment marker is a small extension to process-group cleanup and pidfds prevent PID-reuse signals, but clearing the marker invalidates the guarantee and no cleanup proof catches that condition.\\\"\n    }\n  ],\n  \\\"tools\\\": [\n    {\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"artifact-check\\\",\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"passed\\\",\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"command:\\\\\\\"\"'$POSE_REVIEW_CLI'\"\\\\\\\" artifact-check --spec pose-review-run-reaps-lingering-reviewer-processes --strict\\\",\n      \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"Exited 0. Its slug-wide lineage output reported a broader change set than the sealed bundle; the supplied range and listed paths were reviewed directly.\\\"\n    },\n    {\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"assess-design\\\",\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"passed\\\",\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"structure:design-f569ec881cd9677d\\\",\n      \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"Ran the required design assessment; it reported status observed and no structural deltas.\\\"\n    },\n    {\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"assess-discover\\\",\n      \\\"component\\\": \\\"pose-mcp\\\",\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"passed\\\",\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"command:\\\\\\\"\"'$POSE_REVIEW_CLI'\"\\\\\\\" assess discover --no-persist --component pose-mcp\\\",\n      \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"Ran without persistence; the component was discovered.\\\"\n    },\n    {\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"assess-integrate\\\",\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"passed\\\",\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"integration:pose-mcp/go/delegation-surface-integration\\\",\n      \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"Ran without persistence; three existing HTTP declarations had no observed consumers and no integration gap was introduced by these paths.\\\"\n    },\n    {\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"assess-tech-debt\\\",\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"deferred\\\",\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"command:\\\\\\\"\"'$POSE_REVIEW_CLI'\"\\\\\\\" assess tech-debt --no-persist\\\",\n      \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"Ran, but its scan was incomplete because two unrelated specs had invalid/unknown scope; changed production files have no TODO/FIXME/stub/panic markers.\\\"\n    },\n    {\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"closeout-check\\\",\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"deferred\\\",\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"command:\\\\\\\"\"'$POSE_REVIEW_CLI'\"\\\\\\\" closeout-check spec:pose-review-run-reaps-lingering-reviewer-processes\\\",\n      \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"Deferred because closeout-check requires a completed review attestation, which this brief prohibits recording.\\\"\n    },\n    {\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"review-check\\\",\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"deferred\\\",\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"command:\\\\\\\"\"'$POSE_REVIEW_CLI'\"\\\\\\\" review-check spec:pose-review-run-reaps-lingering-reviewer-processes\\\",\n      \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"Deferred because review-check requires a completed review attestation, which this brief prohibits recording.\\\"\n    },\n    {\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"suggest-review\\\",\n      \\\"component\\\": \\\"pose-mcp\\\",\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"passed\\\",\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"command:\\\\\\\"\"'$POSE_REVIEW_CLI'\"\\\\\\\" suggest review --path pose-mcp\\\",\n      \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"Selected backend-go, security, and documentation-style rules for this component.\\\"\n    },\n    {\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"surface-check\\\",\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"passed\\\",\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"reachability:pose-mcp/go/delivery-reachability\\\",\n      \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"Ran strict surface-check; it reported one target, 236 results, and zero findings.\\\"\n    },\n    {\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"validate\\\",\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"deferred\\\",\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"build:pose-mcp/go/build\\\",\n      \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"Ran strict validation, but the read-only sandbox prevented Go from creating its work directories; sealed build, e2e, integration, and unit evidence covers the matrix. Focused tests, race tests, and vet passed independently.\\\"\n    },\n    {\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"validate\\\",\n      \\\"component\\\": \\\"pose-mcp\\\",\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"deferred\\\",\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"unit:pose-mcp/go/test\\\",\n      \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"Ran module-scoped strict validation, but the read-only sandbox blocked Go build/test work directories; sealed component build and unit evidence remains available. Focused tests, race tests, and vet passed independently.\\\"\n    }\n  ]\n}\n\"'```\nPOSE_REVIEW_FINAL'","aggregated_output":"Draft check: the conclusion step would accept this draft.\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_67","type":"agent_message","text":"decision: changes-requested\n\nThe process group cleanup and abandoned attempt recovery work for the covered cases, and the earlier release race findings are fixed. Two blockers remain: a cleared environment marker can let a descendant survive successful cleanup, and an unreadable active marker can be mistaken for an abandoned markerless reservation. I recorded one low severity observability follow-up.\n\n## Findings\n\n- **N1 — medium, blocker:** [delegation_release.go:197](/var/tmp/pose-work-go/pose-review-run-3562965836/worktree/pose-mcp/internal/pose/delegation_release.go:197) — `orphanReservations` discards losses from `ListDelegationActive`. A damaged live marker can be treated as absent, allowing `--confirm-abandoned` to publish a failed run and receipt without proving the owner is dead.\n- **N2 — high, blocker:** [review_reap_linux.go:74](/var/tmp/pose-work-go/pose-review-run-3562965836/worktree/pose-mcp/internal/pose/review_reap_linux.go:74) — If a descendant escapes the process group and clears `POSE_SEALED_CHECKOUT`, the scan finds no marked process and returns success. The cleanup inventory does not prove that process ended, contrary to L1.\n- **N3 — low, follow-up:** [review_reap_linux.go:61](/var/tmp/pose-work-go/pose-review-run-3562965836/worktree/pose-mcp/internal/pose/review_reap_linux.go:61) — The opaque process count includes a process started during the run, while dispatch records that count as pre-existing processes.\n\n## Criteria\n\n- assumption-integrity — **failed** (N2): L1 names the marker-cleared descendant case, but the code does not prove cleanup fails for it.\n- backend-concurrency — **failed** (N1): a damaged active marker bypasses the owner-dead check on the confirmed orphan path.\n- backend-contracts — **passed**; `integration:pose-mcp/go/delegation-surface-integration`: the CLI flag and failed-run receipt are additive; stored schemas retain their meaning.\n- backend-input-errors — **failed** (N1): marker read loss is dropped during orphan discovery.\n- backend-integration-impact — **passed**; `integration:pose-mcp/go/delegation-surface-integration`: no changed inter-module API; integration scan gaps were unrelated HTTP declarations.\n- backend-observability — **failed** (N3): failure metadata labels the wrong opaque-process count as pre-existing.\n- compatibility — **passed**; `integration:pose-mcp/go/delegation-surface-integration`: existing CLI and ledger contracts remain readable.\n- correctness — **failed** (N2): marker absence is treated as process termination.\n- design-causality — **failed** (N2): D1 addresses separate sessions and D2 preserves ledger history, but clearing D1’s marker defeats the cleanup proof. The design assessment reported no structural deltas.\n- documentation — **passed**; `unit:pose-mcp/go/test`: manuals and scaffold copies describe Linux behavior, and `review-brief/10` asks commands to finish.\n- operability — **failed** (N1): cancel can proceed without surfacing an unreadable marker loss.\n- requirements — **failed** (N2): R1/R2 and the stated L1 behavior are not established for a marker-cleared descendant.\n- scope — **passed**; `unit:pose-mcp/go/test`: the supplied changed paths match the spec artifact list.\n- security — **failed** (N2): a reviewer-started process can evade the mutable marker and survive the run.\n- solution-proportionality — **failed** (N2): environment matching is the smallest extension, but its known invalidating condition is not detected.\n\n## Validation and plan tools\n\n- Focused tests passed: `go -C pose-mcp test ./internal/cli ./internal/pose -run 'DispatchEndsWhatTheReviewer|AbandonedAttempt|RunningAttemptIsNot|Brief'`.\n- Focused concurrency tests passed under `-race`; `go -C pose-mcp vet ./internal/cli ./internal/pose` passed.\n- Both `validate --strict` commands were attempted and stopped because the read-only sandbox could not create Go work directories. This is a run limitation, not a subject defect; the brief seals `build:pose-mcp/go/build`, `unit:pose-mcp/go/test`, and integration/e2e evidence.\n- `surface-check --strict` passed with zero findings. `assess design` reported no structural deltas. `assess integrate` found three unobserved HTTP declarations outside the changed contract. `assess tech-debt` ran but could not read two unrelated specs, so that scan is incomplete.\n- `review-check` and `closeout-check` are deferred until an attestation exists; this review is expressly prohibited from recording one.\n\nNo repository changes or attestation were made.\n\n```pose-draft\n{\n  \"schema\": \"pose.review.draft/v1\",\n  \"decision\": \"changes-requested\",\n  \"findings\": [\n    {\n      \"id\": \"N1\",\n      \"severity\": \"medium\",\n      \"disposition\": \"blocker\",\n      \"file\": \"pose-mcp/internal/pose/delegation_release.go\",\n      \"line\": 197,\n      \"summary\": \"orphanReservations discards unreadable active-marker losses, so a live attempt with a damaged marker can be treated as markerless and released with --confirm-abandoned.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"N2\",\n      \"severity\": \"high\",\n      \"disposition\": \"blocker\",\n      \"file\": \"pose-mcp/internal/pose/review_reap_linux.go\",\n      \"line\": 74,\n      \"summary\": \"A descendant that leaves the process group and clears POSE_SEALED_CHECKOUT is invisible to the scan; no matches is treated as successful cleanup although the process can remain running.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"N3\",\n      \"severity\": \"low\",\n      \"disposition\": \"follow-up\",\n      \"file\": \"pose-mcp/internal/pose/review_reap_linux.go\",\n      \"line\": 61,\n      \"summary\": \"The opaque-process count includes a process started during the run, but dispatch records that count as processes that predated the run.\",\n      \"action\": \"Count only baseline-matched opaque processes in the returned limitation and cover the count in the regression test.\",\n      \"owner\": \"@pose-maintainers\",\n      \"review_by\": \"2026-12-24\"\n    }\n  ],\n  \"prior_findings\": [\n    {\n      \"id\": \"R4-N2\",\n      \"status\": \"fixed\",\n      \"evidence\": \"pose-mcp/internal/pose/delegation_release.go:66-76\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"R5-N1\",\n      \"status\": \"fixed\",\n      \"evidence\": \"pose-mcp/internal/pose/delegation_release.go:66-76\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"R5-N2\",\n      \"status\": \"fixed\",\n      \"evidence\": \"pose-mcp/internal/pose/delegation_release.go:113-127\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"R5-N3\",\n      \"status\": \"fixed\",\n      \"evidence\": \"pose-mcp/internal/pose/delegation_release.go:141-155\"\n    }\n  ],\n  \"sweep\": \"Swept the sealed change paths across Linux process enumeration/pidfd signaling, dispatch cleanup ordering and safety records, marker/reservation/receipt release and locking, delegate list/cancel/help behavior, attempt ledger and round accounting, review-brief/10 with earlier-template compatibility, English and pt-BR manuals and scaffold copies, and the related regression tests.\",\n  \"criteria\": [\n    {\n      \"id\": \"assumption-integrity\",\n      \"disposition\": \"finding\",\n      \"evidence\": \"N2\",\n      \"rationale\": \"The run-specific environment marker is verified for descendants that retain it, but absence of the marker is treated as proof that no descendant remains; the L1 case where a descendant clears it is not proven to make cleanup fail.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"backend-concurrency\",\n      \"disposition\": \"finding\",\n      \"evidence\": \"N1\",\n      \"rationale\": \"The flock serializes releases, but discarded active-marker read losses allow the confirmation path to bypass proof that a live owner is gone.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"backend-contracts\",\n      \"disposition\": \"passed\",\n      \"evidence\": \"integration:pose-mcp/go/delegation-surface-integration\",\n      \"rationale\": \"The new cancel flag is additive, existing record schemas remain unchanged, and released attempts use ordinary failed run and receipt records.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"backend-input-errors\",\n      \"disposition\": \"finding\",\n      \"evidence\": \"N1\",\n      \"rationale\": \"A corrupt or unreadable marker is not surfaced as a release refusal; the orphan scan treats it as absent.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"backend-integration-impact\",\n      \"disposition\": \"passed\",\n      \"evidence\": \"integration:pose-mcp/go/delegation-surface-integration\",\n      \"rationale\": \"The integration assessment found no changed REST, Protobuf, Kafka, or MCP contract; its three unobserved HTTP declarations are outside this change.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"backend-observability\",\n      \"disposition\": \"finding\",\n      \"evidence\": \"N3\",\n      \"rationale\": \"When an opaque process started during the run, the returned count includes it while the dispatch limitation labels the count as pre-existing.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"compatibility\",\n      \"disposition\": \"passed\",\n      \"evidence\": \"integration:pose-mcp/go/delegation-surface-integration\",\n      \"rationale\": \"Existing CLI arguments and stored record meanings are retained; the new confirmation flag and failed-run receipt are additive.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"correctness\",\n      \"disposition\": \"finding\",\n      \"evidence\": \"N2\",\n      \"rationale\": \"The successful no-match path does not establish that all run-owned descendants ended when a descendant clears the marker and leaves the process group.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"design-causality\",\n      \"disposition\": \"finding\",\n      \"evidence\": \"N2\",\n      \"rationale\": \"D1 correctly addresses commands escaping the adapter process group and D2 preserves attempt history, but D1's marker can be cleared and the current cleanup path then has no evidence that the process ended.\",\n      \"mappings\": []\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"documentation\",\n      \"disposition\": \"passed\",\n      \"evidence\": \"unit:pose-mcp/go/test\",\n      \"rationale\": \"The root and scaffold manuals in both locales describe Linux marker-based reaping, stalled-attempt release, and the explicit legacy confirmation; the brief uses immutable review-brief/10.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"operability\",\n      \"disposition\": \"finding\",\n      \"evidence\": \"N1\",\n      \"rationale\": \"The cancel path can release despite an unreadable live marker and does not carry the listing loss into the successful named-attempt path.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"requirements\",\n      \"disposition\": \"finding\",\n      \"evidence\": \"N2\",\n      \"rationale\": \"R1/R2 and the L1 residual require an escaped descendant that cannot be proven ended to keep cleanup incomplete; the marker-cleared path returns success.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"scope\",\n      \"disposition\": \"passed\",\n      \"evidence\": \"unit:pose-mcp/go/test\",\n      \"rationale\": \"The sealed changed-path list matches the spec artifacts; implementation is confined to review cleanup, abandoned-attempt recovery, CLI/help, brief, and manuals.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"security\",\n      \"disposition\": \"finding\",\n      \"evidence\": \"N2\",\n      \"rationale\": \"A reviewer-started process can evade the ownership marker and continue after the run while cleanup reports success; the design relies on a mutable process environment.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"solution-proportionality\",\n      \"disposition\": \"finding\",\n      \"evidence\": \"N2\",\n      \"rationale\": \"The environment marker is a small extension to process-group cleanup and pidfds prevent PID-reuse signals, but clearing the marker invalidates the guarantee and no cleanup proof catches that condition.\"\n    }\n  ],\n  \"tools\": [\n    {\n      \"id\": \"artifact-check\",\n      \"disposition\": \"passed\",\n      \"evidence\": \"command:\\\"$POSE_REVIEW_CLI\\\" artifact-check --spec pose-review-run-reaps-lingering-reviewer-processes --strict\",\n      \"rationale\": \"Exited 0. Its slug-wide lineage output reported a broader change set than the sealed bundle; the supplied range and listed paths were reviewed directly.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"assess-design\",\n      \"disposition\": \"passed\",\n      \"evidence\": \"structure:design-f569ec881cd9677d\",\n      \"rationale\": \"Ran the required design assessment; it reported status observed and no structural deltas.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"assess-discover\",\n      \"component\": \"pose-mcp\",\n      \"disposition\": \"passed\",\n      \"evidence\": \"command:\\\"$POSE_REVIEW_CLI\\\" assess discover --no-persist --component pose-mcp\",\n      \"rationale\": \"Ran without persistence; the component was discovered.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"assess-integrate\",\n      \"disposition\": \"passed\",\n      \"evidence\": \"integration:pose-mcp/go/delegation-surface-integration\",\n      \"rationale\": \"Ran without persistence; three existing HTTP declarations had no observed consumers and no integration gap was introduced by these paths.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"assess-tech-debt\",\n      \"disposition\": \"deferred\",\n      \"evidence\": \"command:\\\"$POSE_REVIEW_CLI\\\" assess tech-debt --no-persist\",\n      \"rationale\": \"Ran, but its scan was incomplete because two unrelated specs had invalid/unknown scope; changed production files have no TODO/FIXME/stub/panic markers.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"closeout-check\",\n      \"disposition\": \"deferred\",\n      \"evidence\": \"command:\\\"$POSE_REVIEW_CLI\\\" closeout-check spec:pose-review-run-reaps-lingering-reviewer-processes\",\n      \"rationale\": \"Deferred because closeout-check requires a completed review attestation, which this brief prohibits recording.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"review-check\",\n      \"disposition\": \"deferred\",\n      \"evidence\": \"command:\\\"$POSE_REVIEW_CLI\\\" review-check spec:pose-review-run-reaps-lingering-reviewer-processes\",\n      \"rationale\": \"Deferred because review-check requires a completed review attestation, which this brief prohibits recording.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"suggest-review\",\n      \"component\": \"pose-mcp\",\n      \"disposition\": \"passed\",\n      \"evidence\": \"command:\\\"$POSE_REVIEW_CLI\\\" suggest review --path pose-mcp\",\n      \"rationale\": \"Selected backend-go, security, and documentation-style rules for this component.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"surface-check\",\n      \"disposition\": \"passed\",\n      \"evidence\": \"reachability:pose-mcp/go/delivery-reachability\",\n      \"rationale\": \"Ran strict surface-check; it reported one target, 236 results, and zero findings.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"validate\",\n      \"disposition\": \"deferred\",\n      \"evidence\": \"build:pose-mcp/go/build\",\n      \"rationale\": \"Ran strict validation, but the read-only sandbox prevented Go from creating its work directories; sealed build, e2e, integration, and unit evidence covers the matrix. Focused tests, race tests, and vet passed independently.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"validate\",\n      \"component\": \"pose-mcp\",\n      \"disposition\": \"deferred\",\n      \"evidence\": \"unit:pose-mcp/go/test\",\n      \"rationale\": \"Ran module-scoped strict validation, but the read-only sandbox blocked Go build/test work directories; sealed component build and unit evidence remains available. Focused tests, race tests, and vet passed independently.\"\n    }\n  ]\n}\n```"}}
